<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Francis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1936">1936</a>–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Jorge Mario Bergoglio</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Francis, born Jorge Mario Bergoglio in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> who served as Archbishop of Buenos Aires from 1998 and was elected pope on 13 March 2013. He was the first pope from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and the first Jesuit pope, and his pontificate stressed care for the poor, migrants and the environment. He died on 21 April 2025.</p></div>
